// recomp_seeds.json — this game's recompiler seeds (external/psxport/tools/recomp/emit.py --seeds).
//
// The recompiler discovers functions from the binary itself: the entry point, the pointer/table scans,
// then the direct-`jal` call graph. What it CANNOT see is anything reached only through a function
// pointer, or entered at a runtime-computed re-entry point, or an overlay's load base. Those are facts
// about THIS executable and THIS disc, so the framework ships none of them and every game supplies its
// own file. JSON with `//` comments; every key is optional.
//
// IT IS EMPTY BECAUSE NOTHING HAS BEEN REVERSE-ENGINEERED (docs/re-frontier.md RE-01, RE-02, RE-03).
//
// Two rules, both learned the hard way elsewhere in this workspace:
//
//   * NEVER copy another game's seed list. A foreign seed that lands inside your text SPLITS a real
//     function at an arbitrary offset — the emit SUCCEEDS and the recomp is silently corrupt. And note
//     that unlike the sibling ports there is no decomp of this game to lift a seed out of even if the
//     rule allowed it: every address here will come out of Ghidra on SLUS_008.93, or out of a
//     `[recomp-MISS] 0x800xxxxx` fail-fast on a booting port.
//   * NEVER guess an overlay base. An overlay is keyed BY its load address, so a wrong base emits a
//     whole module of correctly-decoded instructions at wrong addresses, and every jal target, pointer
//     test and router lookup is then silently wrong. A missing base is a HARD ERROR in emit.py,
//     deliberately — that refusal is the feature.
//
// THIS GAME HAS 21 CODE OVERLAYS (docs/info/claims/002-*): LEVEL01..LEVEL10/{LEVEL,LEVEL1}.BIN (20)
// plus BITS/MEMORY.BIN, 245,148 bytes = 29.1% of the game's code-bearing bytes. LEVEL00/LEVEL.BIN bears
// an overlay name but is a 4-byte placeholder holding no code, and FMV/FMV.BIN — the only other file on
// the disc with a `jr $ra` — is class-UNRESOLVED (RE-04), NOT a known overlay. `tools/base_fit.py` MEASURES
// a load base of 0x800D1000 for 15 of them (75-100% of their own out-of-.text jal targets inside the
// window, 0.0% runner-up) — and that number still does not belong in `overlay_bases` below, because how
// the loader ARRIVES at it is unknown and whether LEVEL.BIN and LEVEL1.BIN share one slot is unresolved.
// RE-03 is where a fitted base becomes a confirmed one. See game/core/game_config.cpp's overlay block.
//
// Grow the main list empirically: boot, and when the substrate fail-fasts with `[recomp-MISS]
// 0x800xxxxx`, add that address WITH a note on how it is reached. An address with no rationale is
// unreviewable later.
{
  "main": [],
  "main_reentry": [],
  "overlay_bases": {},
  "overlay_base_patterns": [],
  "overlay_seeds": {}
}
